/// `unbiased-composition`: a chain of paths composes unbiased at a stratum the chain sub-site certifies.
///
/// Implemented: `compose[n, k](chain(m), (c₁, …, cₘ))` checks its cells against the chain of `m` cells at the stratum `n` over `k`. The node holds its cells beside their left-nested `then` fold. Evaluation runs the fold, and the kernel replays it. `p then q` at paths is the composite of its 2-chain, `compose[3, 5](chain(2), (p, q))`. The printer and the formatter write the form back as it is written, and that composite as `p then q`.
///
/// A composite of reflexivities reduces to reflexivity, so the declaration states it and proves it by reflexivity.
///
/// - see: corpus/model/identity/compose-chain.gandr

/// Three reflexivities composed unbiased are reflexivity.
def composedAtHere(A : Type, x : A) -> Path(
  Path(A, x, x),
  compose[5, 7](chain(3), (here(x), here(x), here(x))),
  here(x)
) {
  here(here(x))
}
